---
import ButtonLink from '../components/ui/ButtonLink.astro';
import Panel from '../components/ui/Panel.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd, personJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Carlos Ulloque | Mission Critical Engineer"
  description="Carlos Ulloque — mission critical infrastructure engineer. Oracle platforms (Exadata, RAC, Data Guard, ZDLRA), recovery and high availability, and security and privacy designed into the system."
  schemas={[
    personJsonLd(),
    breadcrumbJsonLd([
      { name: 'Carlos Ulloque', path: '/' },
      { name: 'About', path: '/about' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-signal">
      Profile
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold text-ink-text">About</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-muted">
      Infrastructure engineer working on Oracle platforms — Exadata, RAC, Data
      Guard, ZDLRA — where availability and recovery are requirements, not
      targets. Day to day that is patching, automation, observability, and
      troubleshooting systems already in production that cannot simply be
      stopped to be fixed.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-muted">
      Most of that experience is in enterprise infrastructure, recovery and
      backup platforms, monitoring, and high-availability designs — where
      stability and recovery time matter as much as performance. The systems
      that hold up are the ones that keep serving while partially degraded, with
      a recovery path defined before the incident rather than improvised during
      it.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-muted">
      The current direction is architectural: bringing infrastructure, security,
      and privacy into the same design instead of treating them as separate
      layers. That means systems built to reduce unnecessary trust and exposure,
      with automation and assistive tooling treated as ordinary parts of an
      operational architecture — kept inside explicit boundaries rather than
      bolted on.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-text">Current focus</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <Panel eyebrow="Infrastructure" title="Mission critical systems">
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6">
          <li>Oracle Exadata / RAC / Data Guard / ZDLRA</li>
          <li>Continuity, recovery, and graceful degradation</li>
          <li>Infrastructure automation and safe re-runs</li>
          <li>Observability and operational tooling</li>
        </ul>
      </Panel>
      <Panel eyebrow="Security" title="Trust & resilience">
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm leading-6">
          <li>Zero Trust and explicit trust boundaries</li>
          <li>Privacy-aware systems with minimal central trust</li>
          <li>Client-side encryption and local ownership of secrets</li>
          <li>Automation and tooling under explicit control</li>
        </ul>
      </Panel>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-text">Explore</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-muted">
      Field notes, engineering projects, and experimental work.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <ButtonLink href="/notes">Technical notes</ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink href="/projects" variant="secondary">Projects</ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink href="/labs" variant="secondary">Labs</ButtonLink>
      <ButtonLink href="/uses" variant="secondary">Uses</ButtonLink>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
